No, we do not disregard the bones levels, because those bones may
contain potions, and those could certainly impact what is happening.  A
sufficiently played server such as NAO has a perpetual supply of bones,
and while I doubt all of them are healers (the most obvious source of
potions), they certainly should be considered.

> Do the amounts of potions on lower levels change?

-- Bones files appear on DL4 and below.

-- Monsters that can be generated with defensive items (healing potions)
are more common on deeper levels.

-- Certain special rooms (barracks) only appear on deeper levels.

-- The player is likely to spend more time on deeper levels for various
reasons, if only because he is passing through them on his way to
somewhere else (returning to the Minetown altar, returning to a stash in
Sokoban, coming back for the Quest, etc), thus increasing the number of
monsters generated on those levels, defensive items on those monsters, 
and hence deathdrops.  The average player is going to visit DL1 once per 
game; the average ascender, twice.  That's not a lot of time spent high
up in the dungeon, and depending on how deep the entrance to the Gnomish
Mines is, you could safely include DL2 or DL3 in this as well.

